// kinetics
// Purpose: millisecond kinetics chip using nanoliter reagents
// (Song / Ismagilov). Buffer, substrate, and RNase A merge to one out.
// Topology: three finputs sum-merge directly onto a single foutput (star merge).
// Collaborators: note typo `subtrate` is intentional in the netlist; do not rename.
// All reagents share one continuous assign path — no storage or MAP stages.

module kinetics(
    finput buffer, subtrate, r_nase_a,   // buffer, substrate (typo preserved), RNase A inlets
    foutput out                          // single merged kinetics product outlet
);

    // Merge all three reagent streams into the outlet on one continuous path.
    assign out = buffer + subtrate + r_nase_a;

endmodule
